#: ../../source/docs/common-aerotate-dronecan-battery.rst:41
#: c1cc1d96c1f44d0eb65c9e6aebadc60e
msgid "The aeroPAX batteries come with a standard adapter to attach to your drone. The adapter comes with standard JST-GH plugs to connect to one of the CAN buses. Current distribution can be done directly on the adapter board. The adapters are customizable, if there is the need, you can contact info@aerotate.de."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-aerotate-dronecan-battery.rst:43
#: 9b7a7d6d8a204830be8606958b6e54b3
msgid "To setup the aeroPAX Smart Battery in Mission Planer for DroneCAN, go to Config/Tuning Full Parameter List, then search for “BATT” or scroll down to :ref:`BATT_MONITOR<BATT_MONITOR>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-aerotate-dronecan-battery.rst:49
#: 028e687e5f95442aa6c14079a0f7beee
msgid "Connect to the autopilot with a ground station and set the following parameters and then reboot the autopilot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-aerotate-dronecan-battery.rst:51
#: 013d3cba86954dfda91e3773aba062cc
msgid "Set :ref:`CAN_P1_DRIVER<CAN_P1_DRIVER>` to 1 (First Driver) or :ref:`CAN_P2_DRIVER<CAN_P2_DRIVER>` to 1 (Second Driver) for second CAN port"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-aerotate-dronecan-battery.rst:52
#: 145eb8c5ec4348ae9724c7d41a1bc596
msgid "Set :ref:`CAN_D1_PROTOCOL<CAN_D1_PROTOCOL>` to 1 (DroneCAN) or :ref:`CAN_D2_PROTOCOL<CAN_D2_PROTOCOL>` to 1 for second CAN port"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-aerotate-dronecan-battery.rst:53
#: 4ba3b4f90bc64a95ba9d1e8e9f7ab7ad
msgid "Set :ref:`BATT_MONITOR<BATT_MONITOR>` to 8 (DroneCAN)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-aerotate-dronecan-battery.rst:54
#: bc14674f55a24ed5b0e25b60ed630151
msgid "Set :ref:`BATT_SERIAL_NUM<BATT_SERIAL_NUM>` to the address you have set at the battery adapter. On each battery adapter, 4 bits can be set to encode this field resulting in 16 possible addresses, where addresses 0 and 15 are reserved and cannot be used. The DroneCAN parameter is battery_id."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-aerotate-dronecan-battery.rst:56
#: 61e342b7b04e4d39a00b775a8ef7f218
msgid "The aeroPAX batteries can be setup in parallel and series, but max 2 in series. For parallel setups, a protected output is strongly recommended. It enables hot-swap-ability and protects against user errors. For parallel setups an additional battery monitor can be added as :ref:`BATT_SUM_MASK<BATT_SUM_MASK>`, this will sum up the currents and average the voltages, for a better overview."
msgstr ""

